# RECIPE chase: a camera that follows a car down the street, then swings in low beside it. Copy this file, change the cars, the route and the numbers.
#
# What it uses: a spot for where the car starts (spots.txt: hw-lane1, lane 1 of the street outside the Hollywood garage gate), a route file for where it
# drives (routes\street-lane1.route, beside this scene), and `rig chase` for the camera (camera.h: dist behind, height up, side to the right, lag in
# seconds). No coordinates are written here: change the spot name to move the shot (a spot with a straight road ahead: spots.txt notes say which).
#
# Timeline (scene seconds from the moment a car is on the road): a spawn takes about 4 s, so the car is ready at about 5 s and the camera
# takes over at 6; the car drives 50 m at 7 m/s (7 s); it stops at its route's end; the game's camera is back at 13.
#   6    chase from behind: 7 m back, 1.9 up, a third of a second of lag, fov 50
#   9    the camera moves to 3.5 m back, 1.1 up, 1.6 m to the right and a tighter lens (ease inout: the segment that starts here is eased)
# To record it: add `at 6 capture fps 60 name my-chase sink png` and `at 13 capture off` (one take a scene).
scene recipe-chase fps 60 step 1/60
world hour 16.5 hold weather nice traffic off peds off parked off police off
at 0 hud off
at 0.5 car p1 spawn vp_lam_murcielago_06 at spot:hw-lane1@0,0,-25 heading spot:hw-lane1
at 6 car p1 path street-lane1.route speed 7
cam 6 rig chase car:p1 dist 7 height 1.9 lag 0.35 fov 50
cam 9 rig chase car:p1 dist 3.5 height 1.1 side 1.6 lag 0.2 fov 42 ease inout
at 13 mark game-camera
cam 13 off
at 13.5 car p1 delete
end 14.5
